# Docs

If the project has no existing documentation convention, use this layout:
`README.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` at the repo root — hosting platforms (GitHub,
npm, package marketplaces) read them from there — and every other doc under
`docs/` at the repo root, linked from `README.md`. If the project already
follows a different convention, match it instead.

Update only when the file already exists and the trigger applies:

- `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` — testable behavior changed.
- `README.md` — usage or configuration changed.
- `docs/DEPLOY.md` — deploy steps, environment variables, or infra config changed.
- `CHANGELOG.md` — release-worthy change, under `[Unreleased]`.
